    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Logistics entrepreneur Travis Burt gave employees a say in how Transportation Impact supported its community. Marketing staff proposed the IMPACT1 programme, and he and co-founder Keith Byrd encouraged participation without making volunteering compulsory. Employees could spend paid working time on causes that mattered to them. The company also offered paid summer half-days, making its coastal location a practical benefit for staff.\n\nEast Carolina University invited Burt to give the keynote address at its first supply-chain summit. He explained the field through everyday goods, from clothing to phones, and encouraged students to use emerging tools and data to solve distribution problems.",
    "html": "<p>Logistics entrepreneur Travis Burt gave employees a say in how Transportation Impact supported its community. Marketing staff proposed the IMPACT1 programme, and he and co-founder Keith Byrd encouraged participation without making volunteering compulsory. Employees could spend paid working time on causes that mattered to them. The company also offered paid summer half-days, making its coastal location a practical benefit for staff.</p>\r\n<p>East Carolina University invited Burt to give the keynote address at its first supply-chain summit. He explained the field through everyday goods, from clothing to phones, and encouraged students to use emerging tools and data to solve distribution problems.</p>\r\n",
